course: dictionary
lesson: 677
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word ball can mean a game object, a round shape, or a party. To choose the right meaning, read the words around it, because they are its context.
explain: «You never kick or throw a ball at someone who is not ready, because it hurts and starts fights.» Kick and throw are the clues. Here a ball is a round thing used in games.
explain: «A family in Ohio left a pan of oil on the hob and went to answer the door; it caught fire, and when someone threw water on it a ball of flame burst up.» No one kicks a ball of flame, so ball means anything round here. Swap in round shape and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Ball is a noun, and its plural is balls.
fact: «Ball» can mean a round thing used in games, for throwing, kicking, hitting or bouncing.
fact: «Ball» can mean anything round, like a ball of wool or a snowball.
fact: «Ball» can also mean a big formal dance party, or the round part under your toes.
fact: To check a meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «You never kick or throw a ball at someone who is not ready, because it hurts and starts fights.» What is a ball here? | A ball of wool | A big formal dance party | *A round thing used in games | The round part under the toes
exercise: «A family in Ohio left a pan of oil on the hob; a ball of flame burst up and burnt the kitchen.» Which meaning of ball fits? | The round part under the toes | A thing used in games | *Anything round, a round burst of fire | A big formal dance party
exercise: «In dried-up pools a lungfish sleeps in a ball of mud until the rain comes back.» What does ball mean here? | A dance held in the pools | *A rounded lump of mud | A game played in mud | A thing thrown at the rain
test: «Those years were like a playground where five bigger kids fight over one ball at once.» Which meaning of ball does this sentence use? | The round part under the toes | A snowball in the snow | A big formal dance party | *A round thing used in games
test: A child says, «We had a ball at the party.» What does have a ball mean? | *Had great fun | Kicked the ball hard | Danced in a formal hall | Caught something round
exam: «The ball of my foot pressed into the sand.» Which meaning of ball is this? | A big formal dance | A round thing used in games | A snowball | *The round part under the toes
